{"task_id": "Mbpp/90", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef len_log(strings: List[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute and return the length of the longest string in strings.\n\n    If strings is empty, return 0. All elements in strings must be of type str; else raise TypeError.\n    String length is determined using Python's built-in len() on str (Unicode codepoint count).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return 0\n\n    max_length = 0\n    for word in strings:\n        if not isinstance(word, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the input list must be strings.\")\n        max_length = max(max_length, len(word))\n    return max_length"}
