{"task_id": "Mbpp/262", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\ndef split_two_parts(input_list: List[Any], L: int) -> Tuple[List[Any], List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into two parts: the first part has length L, and the second part contains the remaining elements.\n    Raises ValueError if L is out of the valid range [0, len(input_list)].\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if not (0 <= L <= list_length):\n        raise ValueError(\"L out of allowed range 0..len(input_list)\")\n\n    first_part = input_list[0:L]\n    second_part = input_list[L:]\n\n    return (first_part, second_part)"}
